A180 — the activation call the macOS 27 SDK is retiring
Host: 27.0 / arm64, SDK 27.0

--- The annotation, from the SDK itself ---
  AppKit.framework/Headers/NSApplication.h:222:- (void)activateIgnoringOtherApps:(BOOL)ignoreOtherApps API_DEPRECATED("This method will be deprecated in a future release. Use NSApp.activate instead.", macos(10.0, API_TO_BE_DEPRECATED));
  224:/// Makes the receiver the active app, if possible.
  225-///
  226-/// You shouldn’t assume the app will be active immediately
  (Nothing warns today: 'to be deprecated' is not 'deprecated', which is why the build with
   warnings-as-errors cannot catch this and a source check can.)

--- BEFORE: the call at HEAD ---
  328:            NSApp.activate(ignoringOtherApps: true)

